'' See the source's header. A boolean compared against something that is not one is
'' WIDENED FIRST -- normalised to its storage value and then negated, so true is -1 --
'' and the pair is compared at INTEGER.
''
'' The assertion is on the negation instruction existing at all: the broken compiler
'' emitted NONE for this file ('= sub ' occurs 0 times; it occurs 4 times now, one per
'' boolean that needed widening). The final 'icmp.eq' reads the same in both, which is
'' why it is not what is asserted on.
''
'' Two of the seven printed lines came out wrong before the fix -- 1 and 4 -- and the
'' other five did not, so a test carrying any of those five alone would pass on it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/bool-vs-nonbool-compare.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: = sub 
